  "isLocked": true,
  "description": "Transform categorical discrete labels into integer indices or orthogonal binary one-hot vectors.\n\nOne-hot encoding avoids imposing artificial ordinal distance relationships between nominal categories, ensuring Euclidean independence.\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n$$\n\\mathbf{e}_{\\text{onehot}}(c) = [\\mathbb{I}(c = u_1), \\dots, \\mathbb{I}(c = u_K)]\n$$\n\n### Step-by-Step Implementation\n1. Extract sorted unique categories from categorical column\n2. Construct integer mapping dictionary cat_to_id\n3. Generate label-encoded integers or sparse binary one-hot vectors\n\n### Returns\nDictionary with 'categories' and 'encoded'.",
  "theory": "## Understanding the Theory: Categorical Encoding\n\n### Core Intuition: Why Do We Need This?\nIn computational mathematics and machine learning, robust algorithmic routines ensure calculations are both mathematically sound and computationally efficient. **Categorical Encoding** implements a core computational building block.\n\nOne-hot encoding avoids imposing artificial ordinal distance relationships between nominal categories, ensuring Euclidean independence. In this problem, the goal is to: transform categorical discrete labels into integer indices or orthogonal binary one-hot vectors.\n\n### Mathematical Principles & Formulation\nThe core governing equation for this operation is:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{e}_{\\text{onehot}}(c) = [\\mathbb{I}(c = u_1), \\dots, \\mathbb{I}(c = u_K)]\n$$\n\nEvery term in this formulation plays a precise mathematical role in ensuring dimensional consistency, numerical stability, and correct algorithmic behavior.\n\n### Step-by-Step Computational Workflow\n1. **Phase 1**: Extract sorted unique categories from categorical column\n2. **Phase 2**: Construct integer mapping dictionary cat_to_id\n3. **Phase 3**: Generate label-encoded integers or sparse binary one-hot vectors\n\n### Practical Machine Learning Applications & Nuances\n* **Algorithmic Complexity**: Designing routines with optimal time and space complexity ensures they scale gracefully to large datasets.\n* **Numerical Accuracy**: Safeguarding calculations against floating-point underflow or division by zero ensures consistent results.\n* **Vectorization**: Implementing operations with contiguous array buffers avoids interpreter overhead.",
  "examples": [
    "Input: categories = [\"cat\", \"dog\", \"cat\", \"bird\"], method = \"one_hot\"\n\nOutput: {\"categories\": [\"bird\", \"cat\", \"dog\"], \"encoded\": [[0, 1, 0], [0, 0, 1], [0, 1, 0], [1, 0, 0]]}\n\nExplanation: Evaluated ml_categorical_encoding under standard test conditions."
  ],
  "requirements": "* Function must be named `ml_categorical_encoding`\n* Return value must match the exact expected structure and types\n* Handle edge cases cleanly and maintain numerical stability\n* Must run efficiently without redundant memory allocations",
