  "starterCode": "def ml_categorical_encoding(categories: list, method: str = 'one_hot') -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Categorical Encoding** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\ndef ml_categorical_encoding(categories: list, method: str = 'one_hot') -> dict:\n    u = sorted(list(set(categories)))\n    c2i = {c: i for i, c in enumerate(u)}\n    if method == 'label': enc = [c2i[c] for c in categories]\n    else:\n        enc = []\n        for c in categories:\n            r = [0] * len(u); r[c2i[c]] = 1; enc.append(r)\n    return {'categories': u, 'encoded': enc}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
